H("601.d.1.D",4,"Answering a negative online review politely and offering to make things right is an example of good:","public relations",["food costing","knife work","inventory"],"PR protects a business's reputation.")
H("601.d.2",3,"When a team cannot agree on a catering menu, a critical thinker should first:","gather facts and weigh the options",["flip a coin","pick the loudest idea","walk away"],"Critical thinking weighs evidence before deciding.")
H("601.d.2",4,"A freezer fails during service. Which response best shows advanced problem solving?","move food to working units and log the temperatures",["serve everything anyway","blame the last shift","close for the week"],"A solution protects safety and records evidence.")
H("601.d.3.A",3,"OSHA's Hazard Communication rule requires kitchens to label cleaning chemicals and keep:","safety data sheets",["old receipts","guest surveys","menu drafts"],"SDS explain chemical hazards and first aid.")
H("601.d.3.A",4,"To comply with OSHA, employers must provide protective gear such as cut-resistant gloves and:","training on using it",["free lunches","extra breaks only","private offices"],"Training goes with equipment.")
H("601.d.3.B",3,"After a coworker is burned, the first step in a proper incident procedure is to give first aid and notify a:","supervisor",["customer","vendor","reporter"],"Supervisors start the reporting process.")
H("601.d.3.B",4,"Writing an accident report helps a business find the cause so the event does not:","happen again",["get praised","raise the menu price","need training"],"Reports guide prevention.")
H("601.d.3.C",3,"Getting enough sleep before a long banquet shift is a wellness habit that improves:","alertness",["menu prices","hiring","parking"],"Rest keeps workers focused.")
H("601.d.3.C",4,"A cook with a fever and vomiting should report it and stay home to protect coworkers and:","food safety",["tip income","menu design","decor"],"Sick workers can spread illness through food.")
H("601.d.3.D",3,"A rule that all staff must wear closed-toe, non-slip shoes in the kitchen helps prevent:","falls and burns",["boredom","late arrivals","menu errors"],"Proper footwear protects feet and balance.")
H("601.d.3.D",4,"Calling 'Behind!' when passing another worker with a hot pan follows a workplace:","safety rule",["pricing policy","dress style","hiring method"],"Announcing your movement prevents collisions.")
H("601.d.4.A",3,"A cook who arrives early, stays busy, and helps others without being asked shows a positive:","work ethic",["rumor","grudge","excuse"],"Productive effort reflects work ethic.")
H("601.d.4.A",4,"Which attitude leads to a more productive kitchen?","taking initiative to restock before rush",["waiting to be told everything","complaining about tasks","leaving early quietly"],"Initiative keeps work flowing.")
H("601.d.4.B",3,"A cook notices a pricing mistake in the guest's favor and tells the manager. This shows:","integrity",["laziness","greed","deceit"],"Honesty when no one is watching is integrity.")
H("601.d.4.B",4,"Choosing the ethical course sometimes means admitting a mistake, such as a dropped tray, instead of:","hiding it",["fixing it","reporting it","learning from it"],"Honesty builds trust.")
H("601.d.4.C",3,"A restaurant must follow health codes, labor laws, and local:","ordinances",["fashions","rumors","menus"],"Businesses comply with rules at every level of government.")
H("601.d.4.C",4,"Paying workers for overtime hours is required to comply with:","labor laws",["menu trends","dress codes","parking rules"],"Pay rules are set by law.")
H("601.d.5.A",3,"Before using a commercial slicer, a student should be trained, wear cut protection, and always use the:","blade guard",["bare hands","wet cloth","oven mitt"],"Guards prevent serious cuts.")
H("601.d.5.A",4,"A tilting skillet, stand mixer, and convection oven are all examples of commercial:","equipment",["garnishes","recipes","uniforms"],"Equipment varies in size and function.")
H("601.d.5.B",3,"Adding a fresh herb sprig to a finished entrée is a presentation technique called:","garnishing",["receiving","proofing","blanching"],"Garnish adds color and flavor to the plate.")
H("601.d.5.B",4,"A plate with height, contrasting colors, and clean edges is more likely to appear:","professional",["careless","rushed","dull"],"Neat, balanced plating shows skill.")
H("601.d.5.C",3,"Poaching an egg in simmering water uses which cooking category?","moist heat",["dry heat","combination","no heat"],"Poaching cooks in liquid.")
H("601.d.5.C",4,"Sautéing vegetables in a hot pan with a little oil is a:","dry-heat method",["moist-heat method","raw method","cold method"],"Fat, not water, carries the heat.")
H("601.d.5.D",3,"Making a roux from equal parts flour and butter by weight is an advanced skill used to thicken:","sauces",["salads","ice","coffee"],"Roux is a classic thickener.")
H("601.d.5.D",4,"Reducing a stock by simmering it concentrates its:","flavor",["volume","water","fat only"],"Evaporation concentrates flavor.")
H("601.d.5.E",3,"Allowing shaped dough to rest and rise before baking is called:","proofing",["blanching","searing","glazing"],"Proofing lets yeast inflate the dough.")
H("601.d.5.E",4,"Laminated doughs such as croissants get flaky layers from folding in:","butter",["salt","yeast only","sugar syrup"],"Butter layers separate the dough as it bakes.")
H("601.d.5.F",3,"Under FIFO storage, the oldest products in the walk-in are used:","first",["last","never","only at night"],"FIFO prevents spoilage.")
H("601.d.5.F",4,"Raw meat belongs on the lowest storage shelf so its juices cannot drip onto:","ready-to-eat food",["the floor mat","the shelf label","the freezer door"],"Lower placement prevents cross-contamination.")
H("601.d.5.G",3,"A three-compartment sink is used in the order wash, rinse, and:","sanitize",["dry","soak","scrape"],"Sanitizing is the final step before air drying.")
H("601.d.5.G",4,"Equipment cleaning schedules and checklists help a kitchen stay:","consistently clean",["very quiet","over budget","understaffed"],"Schedules make cleaning routine and accountable.")

# ---- 602 Hospitality practicum (part A) ----
H("602.d.1.A",3,"For hotel front desk employees, professional grooming and appearance help create a good first:","impression",["expense","delay","error"],"Guests judge a business by how staff present themselves.")
H("602.d.1.A",4,"Which is part of appropriate grooming for a hospitality uniform?","clean, pressed clothing and neat hair",["wrinkled shirt","strong perfume","visible stains"],"Neatness shows professionalism.")
H("602.d.1.B",3,"Arriving at work a few minutes early shows:","punctuality",["laziness","rivalry","greed"],"Being on time shows respect for the team.")
H("602.d.1.B",4,"A housekeeper who spots a low supply of towels and restocks them without being asked shows:","initiative",["delay","avoidance","rivalry"],"Initiative means acting without being told.")
H("602.d.1.C",3,"Greeting every guest politely, no matter their background, shows respect for:","diversity",["uniformity","rumors","shortcuts"],"Hospitality welcomes all kinds of people.")
H("602.d.1.C",4,"Positive interpersonal skills include listening, courtesy, and:","empathy",["sarcasm","gossip","impatience"],"Empathy helps workers understand others.")
H("602.d.1.D",3,"Guests may differ in language, culture, age, and ability. These are types of:","diversity",["tardiness","similarity","inventory"],"Diversity covers many human differences.")
H("602.d.1.D",4,"From an employer's view, a diverse staff can help a hotel better serve:","a wide range of guests",["only local guests","one age group","only business travelers"],"Different backgrounds help meet different needs.")
H("602.d.1.E",3,"Using 'please' and 'thank you' and holding a door for a guest are examples of:","etiquette",["inventory","pricing","maintenance"],"Etiquette is polite behavior.")
H("602.d.1.E",4,"Which is correct business etiquette when meeting a client?","a firm handshake and eye contact",["a limp wave","looking at your phone","using slang"],"Professional greetings are confident and respectful.")
H("602.d.1.F",3,"Employees who stay organized, positive, and honest are building strong:","work habits",["debts","costumes","rumors"],"Good habits support success on the job.")
H("602.d.1.F",4,"A bellhop who always has a positive attitude, even on busy days, helps create a:","pleasant guest experience",["quiet lobby","lower price","shorter shift"],"Attitude affects how guests feel.")
H("602.d.1.G",3,"Lifting luggage with your legs instead of your back is an example of personal and occupational:","safety",["style","rivalry","fashion"],"Proper lifting prevents injury.")
H("602.d.1.G",4,"Reporting a wet floor in a hotel lobby protects both employees and:","guests",["competitors","vendors","banks"],"Safety covers everyone in the building.")
H("602.d.1.H",3,"When the front desk and housekeeping share information about room status, they are working to:","support the organization",["slow guests down","hide problems","raise prices"],"Collaboration keeps operations on track.")
H("602.d.1.H",4,"Helping a coworker from another department during a rush shows:","cooperation",["rivalry","avoidance","blame"],"Teams help each other reach shared goals.")
H("602.d.1.I",3,"Using a to-do list to finish tasks before checkout time shows how to organize work to meet:","deadlines",["rumors","budgets","contracts"],"Planning helps tasks get done on time.")
H("602.d.1.I",4,"Doing the most urgent task first is an example of setting:","priorities",["traps","debts","errors"],"Prioritizing keeps important work on schedule.")
H("602.d.1.J",3,"Exercise, balanced meals, and sleep support physical health, while hobbies and relaxation support:","mental health",["menu design","guest rooms","payroll"],"Both kinds of health affect job success.")
H("602.d.1.J",4,"Comparing stress-relief strategies means looking at how each one affects:","body and mind",["room rates","parking","laundry"],"Wellness strategies are judged by their effects.")
H("602.d.2.A",3,"Refusing to take credit for work you did not do is a way to defend personal:","integrity",["wealth","fame","speed"],"Honesty protects your integrity.")
H("602.d.2.A",4,"A desk clerk who tells a manager about a billing error that favors the hotel is defending:","personal integrity",["company secrets","guest rooms","room rates"],"Doing right when it costs something shows integrity.")
H("602.d.2.B",3,"Trust, communication, and respect are characteristics of successful working:","relationships",["conflicts","excuses","bills"],"Good coworkers build good relationships.")
H("602.d.2.B",4,"Teamwork in a hotel means each department shares responsibility for:","guest satisfaction",["individual credit","hiding errors","competing"],"Everyone contributes to the guest's stay.")
H("602.d.2.C",3,"Typical employer expectations include honesty, dependability, and:","following policies",["gossip","tardiness","complaining"],"Employers expect staff to follow the rules.")
H("602.d.2.C",4,"An employee who understands why the employer requires uniforms can better defend that expectation as part of the hotel's:","brand image",["bonus","calendar","budget"],"Uniforms support the professional image of the business.")
H("602.d.2.D",3,"Knocking and announcing yourself before entering a guest room shows respect for the guest's:","privacy",["wealth","luggage","luck"],"Rights to privacy are part of respectful service.")
H("602.d.2.D",4,"A worker who listens to a coworker's opinion even when disagreeing shows respect for the other person's:","rights",["mistakes","pay","tips"],"Respect includes the right to be heard.")
H("602.d.2.E",3,"A hospitality code of ethics is a written set of standards for:","professional conduct",["room decorations","menu prices","parking fees"],"Codes tell workers how to behave ethically.")
H("602.d.2.E",4,"Treating all guests fairly, respecting confidentiality, and being honest in advertising are typical parts of a:","code of ethics",["room rate card","job posting","menu"],"Ethical standards guide professional choices.")
H("602.d.2.F",3,"A hotel policy says employees must clock in and out personally. Following it supports the organization's:","procedures",["rumors","décor","menus"],"Policies keep operations consistent.")
H("602.d.2.F",4,"Following a written procedure for key control helps protect guests and:","hotel property",["room service","parking","pool hours"],"Rules protect people and assets.")
H("602.d.3.A",3,"A hotel clerk calculating a guest's bill with room charge, tax, and a $15 parking fee is using math in:","business transactions",["sports","music","art"],"Everyday work often involves money calculations.")
H("602.d.3.A",4,"A room costs $120 per night with 10 percent tax added. The total for one night is:","$132",["$130","$120","$12"],"10 percent of 120 is 12; 120 + 12 = 132.")
H("602.d.3.B",3,"A bar graph showing room occupancy by month helps managers see:","seasonal trends",["guest names","staff birthdays","room colors"],"Charts reveal patterns in data.")
H("602.d.3.B",4,"If a table shows occupancy of 60 of 80 rooms, the occupancy rate is:","75 percent",["60 percent","80 percent","25 percent"],"60 divided by 80 equals 0.75.")
H("602.d.3.C",3,"A short written message that states who, what, when, and where for a staff meeting is a workplace:","memo",["menu","poem","recipe"],"Memos share information within an organization.")
H("602.d.3.C",4,"Before sending a business letter to a vendor, you should check the tone, accuracy, and:","grammar and spelling",["font color only","paper weight","stamp price"],"Professional documents must be clear and correct.")
H("602.d.4.A",3,"Comparing the published attendance policies of two employers helps you understand how each handles:","absences",["menus","décor","parking"],"Policies explain employer expectations.")
H("602.d.4.A",4,"A published workplace policy is usually found in the employee:","handbook",["menu","guest register","invoice"],"Handbooks collect policies in one place.")
H("602.d.4.B",3,"Reporting a coworker's theft of hotel supplies rather than ignoring it is a(n):","responsible and ethical act",["breach of trust","unfair act","careless habit"],"Honest reporting protects the business.")
H("602.d.4.B",4,"Using a hotel's computers for personal shopping while on the clock is:","an unethical use of time",["a benefit","a sign of initiative","a company policy"],"Employees are paid to use work time for work.")
H("602.d.4.C",3,"The Fair Labor Standards Act is an example of a federal law that governs:","wages and hours",["room design","menu prices","hotel names"],"The FLSA sets minimum wage and overtime rules.")
H("602.d.4.C",4,"State labor laws may require meal and rest breaks in addition to:","federal requirements",["bonuses","tips","uniforms"],"States can add protections beyond federal law.")
H("602.d.4.D",3,"A fiduciary responsibility means putting the customer's interests and money:","in good, honest care",["last","aside for yourself","at risk"],"Fiduciaries act with trust and care.")
H("602.d.4.D",4,"An employee who handles guest payments has a duty to protect that money and follow:","financial policies",["rumors","trends","fashions"],"Employers and employees are trusted with customers' funds.")
H("602.d.5.A",3,"Introducing yourself to new team members and learning their strengths helps build:","teamwork",["rivalry","delays","gossip"],"Team-building starts with good relationships.")
H("602.d.5.A",4,"A student organization's service project can help members practice team-building and interpersonal:","skills",["debts","rivalries","gossip"],"Group projects build teamwork.")
H("602.d.5.B",3,"Running for chapter office in a career and technical student organization is a way to model:","leadership",["avoidance","delay","gossip"],"Officers practice leading others.")
H("602.d.5.B",4,"Planning a fundraiser for a hospitality club lets students apply leadership and:","organizational skills",["gossip","rumors","secrecy"],"Events require planning and leading.")

# ---- 602 Hospitality practicum (part B) ----
H("602.d.6.A",3,"Tourism growth in a region often leads to more openings for hotel and attraction jobs. This describes future:","employment",["taxation","weather","fashion"],"Growth in an industry creates job demand.")
H("602.d.6.A",4,"A reliable source for projected job growth in lodging careers is a government labor:","statistics report",["rumor","menu","coupon"],"Official statistics forecast hiring trends.")
H("602.d.6.B",3,"A person who opens a small bed-and-breakfast is developing an:","entrepreneurial opportunity",["employee benefit","tax refund","guest policy"],"Entrepreneurs start their own businesses.")
H("602.d.6.B",4,"Before starting a tour company, an entrepreneur should study the market, startup costs, and:","legal requirements",["school mascots","moon phases","bus colors"],"Research reduces business risk.")
H("602.d.6.C",3,"When comparing two hotel jobs, the best comparison includes salary, job demands, and:","challenges",["room colors","lobby music","parking spots"],"Total fit includes pay and working conditions.")
H("602.d.6.C",4,"A job with a higher salary but unpredictable late-night shifts shows that every position has pay as well as:","trade-offs",["rewards only","no costs","equal hours"],"Higher pay can come with tougher demands.")
H("602.d.6.D",3,"Changes such as online booking and international travel reflect the changing global:","workplace",["weather","climate","menu"],"Technology and travel shape modern hospitality.")
H("602.d.6.D",4,"Because guests now come from many countries, hospitality workers benefit from learning about other:","cultures",["time zones only","tax rates only","uniform brands"],"Cultural awareness improves service.")
H("602.d.7.A",3,"Taking a college course in hotel management after high school is an example of continuing:","education",["vacation","recreation","negotiation"],"More training opens up better jobs.")
H("602.d.7.A",4,"Earning an industry certificate while working can help an employee qualify for a:","promotion",["layoff","suspension","penalty"],"Certification shows added skills.")
H("602.d.7.B",3,"A professional way to leave a job is to put your resignation in writing and give:","proper notice",["no warning","an insult","a complaint post"],"Proper notice keeps a good reputation.")
H("602.d.7.B",4,"To secure a job, an applicant should prepare a resume, complete applications, and practice for the:","interview",["lottery","vacation","tax audit"],"Interviews decide who is hired.")
H("602.d.8.A",3,"In a full-service hotel, the department that prepares and serves meals is called:","food and beverage",["housekeeping","engineering","security"],"Food and beverage runs restaurants and room service.")
H("602.d.8.A",4,"Cleaning rooms and handling linens is the function of which hotel department?","housekeeping",["front office","sales","accounting"],"Housekeeping keeps rooms ready for guests.")
H("602.d.8.B",3,"An employee who shows proficiency in a department can perform its duties accurately and:","independently",["slowly","rarely","carelessly"],"Proficiency means skilled, reliable work.")
H("602.d.8.B",4,"Handling reservations, check-in, and billing are core duties of the hotel's:","front office",["engineering department","laundry","banquet kitchen"],"The front office manages guest records and payments.")
H("602.d.8.C",3,"Comparing a luxury resort with an economy motel is a comparison of different lodging:","properties",["menus","uniforms","vehicles"],"Properties differ in price, services, and amenities.")
H("602.d.8.C",4,"An extended-stay hotel often offers kitchenettes, which suits guests who need lodging for:","weeks at a time",["a single hour","a few minutes","only holidays"],"Extended-stay suits long visits.")
H("602.d.8.D",3,"A hotel that is part of a large brand but owned by an independent person who pays fees to use the brand is a:","franchise",["chain-owned property","hostel","timeshare"],"Franchise owners license a brand name.")
H("602.d.8.D",4,"In a chain-operated hotel, the parent company usually:","owns and manages the property",["only licenses the logo","pays no staff","has no standards"],"Chain-run properties are controlled by the company.")
H("602.d.8.E",3,"Which is a job in travel and tourism?","tour guide",["welder","surgeon","farmer"],"Tour guides lead visitors through attractions.")
H("602.d.8.E",4,"Selling tickets and operating rides at a theme park are duties in which hospitality area?","amusement and attractions",["banking","construction","manufacturing"],"Theme parks are part of the attractions sector.")
H("602.d.9.A",3,"Terms like 'occupancy,' 'rack rate,' and 'no-show' are examples of job-specific technical:","vocabulary",["recipes","furniture","uniforms"],"Each field has its own terms.")
H("602.d.9.A",4,"A guest who reserves a room but never arrives or cancels is called a:","no-show",["walk-in","upgrade","early bird"],"No-shows can cost a hotel revenue.")
H("602.d.9.B",3,"Entering a guest's name, dates, and room type into the reservation system is a technical procedure for meeting:","guest needs",["staff schedules","tax laws","inventory counts"],"Accurate records support good service.")
H("602.d.9.B",4,"The price a hotel charges per night for a room is called the:","rate",["tax","tip","fine"],"Rate assignment is part of registration.")
H("602.d.9.C",3,"A company that organizes conferences, weddings, and corporate gatherings is an event or:","meeting planning company",["landscaping firm","dental office","bakery"],"Planners coordinate details of gatherings.")
H("602.d.9.C",4,"A new event company's plan should list its services, target clients, and:","pricing",["favorite songs","hobbies","pets"],"Business plans describe what and for whom.")
H("602.d.9.D",3,"Keyless entry using a phone app is an emerging technology that can improve:","guest convenience",["room taxes","laundry loads","lobby noise"],"New tech can speed up check-in.")
H("602.d.9.D",4,"Online review sites have changed how hotels manage their:","reputation",["laundry","building codes","elevators"],"Guests share opinions publicly online.")
H("602.d.9.E",3,"The hotel guest cycle begins with the pre-arrival stage, which includes:","making a reservation",["checking out","leaving feedback","returning keys"],"The cycle starts before the guest arrives.")
H("602.d.9.E",4,"In the traditional guest cycle, which stage comes after arrival?","occupancy",["reservation","departure","pre-arrival"],"Arrival, occupancy, then departure.")
H("602.d.10.B",3,"Presenting a portfolio to an interviewer is a chance to show your skills and:","professionalism",["rivalry","fatigue","gossip"],"Presentations highlight strengths.")
H("602.d.10.B",4,"When explaining a portfolio item, you should describe what you did and what you:","learned",["owed","hid","lost"],"Reflection shows growth.")
H("602.d.10.C",3,"Besides pay, a good job offer might include health insurance, paid time off, and:","retirement contributions",["longer shifts","extra duties","less training"],"Benefits add value.")
H("602.d.10.C",4,"Which offer is worth more if all else is equal?","a $40,000 salary plus health insurance",["a $40,000 salary alone","a $39,000 salary alone","a $38,000 salary with no breaks"],"Benefits increase total compensation.")
H("602.d.10.E",3,"Listing monthly income and all expenses in a plan to track spending is a personal:","budget",["resume","contract","brochure"],"Budgets organize money use.")
H("602.d.10.E",4,"If you earn $2,000 a month and spend $1,700, your savings for the month are:","$300",["$17","$3,700","$2,000"],"2,000 minus 1,700 equals 300.")
H("602.d.10.A.i",3,"The first thing most employers want to see in a portfolio is a current:","resume",["menu","coupon","recipe"],"A resume summarizes your experience.")
H("602.d.10.A.i",4,"A current resume should list your education, skills, and work:","experience",["hobbies only","complaints","old grades"],"Resumes highlight qualifications.")
H("602.d.10.A.ii",3,"A signed checklist showing you mastered technical tasks is official documentation of skill:","competencies",["rumors","fashions","costs"],"This documents what you can do.")
H("602.d.10.A.ii",4,"A teacher-signed skills record in a portfolio shows employers that you have:","proven abilities",["free time","a vacation","a loan"],"Verified records are credible.")
H("602.d.10.A.iii",3,"A scholarship letter and a student-of-the-month certificate are examples of portfolio:","recognitions",["bills","contracts","menus"],"They show achievement.")
H("602.d.10.A.iii",4,"Including awards in a portfolio helps show that others value your:","accomplishments",["mistakes","delays","debts"],"Awards back up your claims.")
H("602.d.10.A.iv",3,"Volunteering to serve meals at a shelter is a community service activity worth listing because it shows:","civic responsibility",["selfishness","avoidance","laziness"],"Service shows character.")
H("602.d.10.A.iv",4,"Employers like to see volunteer hours because they show a commitment to:","helping others",["avoiding work","spending money","tardiness"],"Service reflects values.")
H("602.d.10.A.v",3,"Membership and offices in a career and technical student organization show:","leadership and involvement",["boredom","absence","rivalry"],"Participation shows initiative.")
H("602.d.10.A.v",4,"Competition ribbons from a hospitality skills event belong in the section on student:","organization participation",["housing costs","tax returns","banking"],"They show involvement and skill.")
H("602.d.10.A.vi",3,"A written review from the person who directed your practicum is a supervisor:","evaluation",["menu","invoice","itinerary"],"Evaluations describe your work performance.")
H("602.d.10.A.vi",4,"Strong practicum evaluations in a portfolio provide employers with proof of your:","work performance",["spending habits","travel plans","family size"],"They show how you did on the job.")
H("602.d.10.A.vii",3,"A letter written by a former supervisor to support your job application is a letter of:","recommendation",["resignation","complaint","apology"],"References vouch for you.")
H("602.d.10.A.vii",4,"Before listing someone as a reference or asking for a letter, you should first:","ask their permission",["surprise them","assume yes","copy their words"],"Courtesy comes first.")
H("602.d.10.A.viii",3,"A one-page letter that introduces you and explains why you are a good fit for a specific job is a:","cover letter",["receipt","menu","timetable"],"Cover letters accompany resumes.")
H("602.d.10.A.viii",4,"A strong cover letter should be addressed to the hiring manager and tailored to the:","position",["weather","dress code","parking lot"],"Customize each letter for the job.")
H("602.d.10.A.ix",3,"Proof that you studied for a food handler or sanitation exam is documentation of preparation for industry:","certification",["relocation","marketing","budgeting"],"Certification shows industry-recognized knowledge.")
H("602.d.10.A.ix",4,"Including a certificate from a food safety course in a hospitality portfolio shows employers you understand:","sanitation standards",["room pricing","tour routes","guest feedback"],"Safety training matters in food service.")
H("602.d.10.A.x",3,"A photo of an event you helped plan could be included as another supporting:","document",["expense","rumor","penalty"],"Extra evidence can strengthen a portfolio.")
H("602.d.10.A.x",4,"Anything extra added to a portfolio should be relevant and show your:","qualifications",["secrets","complaints","debts"],"Only relevant, positive items belong.")
H("602.d.10.D.i",3,"Health coverage and retirement contributions that an employer provides are called employee:","benefits",["fines","fees","debts"],"Insurance and benefits affect real income.")
H("602.d.10.D.i",4,"When comparing job offers, a higher salary with no health coverage can cost you more in:","out-of-pocket expenses",["interest earned","bonus pay","tax refunds"],"Lacking insurance can be expensive.")
H("602.d.10.D.ii",3,"Money withheld from a paycheck to fund government programs is a:","tax",["tip","gift","bonus"],"Taxes reduce take-home pay.")
H("602.d.10.D.ii",4,"Your net pay is your gross pay minus taxes and other:","deductions",["additions","tips","raises"],"Net pay is what you take home.")
H("602.d.10.D.iii",3,"Putting money into an account for use after you stop working is saving for:","retirement",["vacation","rent","lunch"],"Starting early lets savings grow.")
H("602.d.10.D.iii",4,"A 401(k) is a common employer-sponsored plan for:","retirement savings",["short-term loans","credit cards","insurance claims"],"It helps workers save for later life.")
H("602.d.10.D.iv",3,"If a job requires moving to another city, you must consider costs such as movers, deposits, and travel. These are:","relocation costs",["tax credits","bonuses","gifts"],"Moves cost money.")
H("602.d.10.D.iv",4,"Before accepting an out-of-state hotel job, you should find out whether the employer will help pay for:","moving expenses",["parking tickets","phone games","vacations"],"Some employers offer relocation help.")
H("602.d.10.D.v",3,"A plan that compares expected income with planned spending is a:","budget",["resume","ledger entry","menu"],"Budgets guide money decisions.")
H("602.d.10.D.v",4,"The first step in making a budget is to figure out your monthly:","income",["vacation","debts to avoid","tips to give"],"You can't plan spending without knowing what you earn.")
H("602.d.10.D.vi",3,"A common guideline is that rent or mortgage should be no more than about 30 percent of your:","income",["savings goal","car value","tax refund"],"Housing is usually the largest expense.")
H("602.d.10.D.vi",4,"Besides rent, housing costs include utilities, insurance, and:","maintenance",["entertainment","tips","souvenirs"],"Ongoing housing expenses add up.")
H("602.d.10.D.vii",3,"Gas, insurance, and repairs are part of a worker's:","transportation costs",["housing costs","tax deductions","retirement plan"],"Getting to work has a price.")
H("602.d.10.D.vii",4,"Taking the bus instead of owning a car can reduce a budget's cost for:","transportation",["groceries","rent","tuition"],"Choice of transportation affects spending.")

# ---- 603 Hospitality practicum II ----
H("603.d.1.A",3,"A hotel clerk smiles, makes eye contact, and says, 'Welcome, how may I help you?' Together the smile and the words show:","verbal and non-verbal communication",["only written communication","no communication","only electronic messaging"],"Words and body language work together.")
H("603.d.1.A",4,"A guest says 'fine' but frowns and sighs. The clerk should recognize that the guest's body language may:","contradict the words",["match the words","be meaningless","prove satisfaction"],"Non-verbal cues can reveal true feelings.")
H("603.d.1.B",3,"Explaining a new check-in process to coworkers in a quick huddle is an example of presenting information:","informally",["in writing only","by contract","through a lawyer"],"A quick team talk is informal.")
H("603.d.1.B",4,"A scheduled slide presentation to hotel investors is a(n):","formal presentation",["casual conversation","text thread","hallway chat"],"Formal talks are planned and structured.")
H("603.d.1.C",3,"Reading guest comment cards and drawing conclusions about common complaints is a way to analyze and interpret:","information",["recipes","tips","laundry"],"Analysis turns data into useful findings.")
H("603.d.1.C",4,"After studying survey results, a manager shares the main findings in a clear summary so staff can:","act on them",["ignore them","hide them","delete them"],"Communication leads to action.")
H("603.d.1.D",3,"Looking at the speaker, avoiding interruptions, and summarizing what was said are habits of:","active listening",["passive hearing","daydreaming","multitasking"],"Active listening requires attention.")
H("603.d.1.D",4,"A guest explains a problem at the desk. The best first response is to:","listen fully before answering",["interrupt with a solution","check the phone","look away"],"Listening first prevents misunderstandings.")
H("603.d.1.E",3,"Thanking guests for feedback and handling complaints calmly are examples of strong:","public relations",["inventory","accounting","scheduling"],"PR builds goodwill.")
H("603.d.1.E",4,"A hotel that supports a local charity event is practicing public relations by improving its image in the:","community",["laundry","kitchen","parking lot"],"Community involvement builds reputation.")
H("603.d.2",3,"A reservation system crashes during check-in. A calm, logical approach is to use a backup process while staff work to:","identify and fix the cause",["blame guests","close the hotel","guess at rates"],"Problem solving finds causes and solutions.")
H("603.d.2",4,"When a team faces a tough scheduling conflict, using critical thinking in a group means:","weighing everyone's input with facts",["picking whoever speaks loudest","avoiding the topic","voting without discussion"],"Groups decide best with evidence.")
H("603.d.3.A",3,"A rule requiring housekeepers to use proper gloves with chemicals is a workplace:","safety rule",["rate policy","menu item","parking rule"],"Rules protect workers from harm.")
H("603.d.3.A",4,"Keeping cleaning carts out of hallways during busy times follows safety rules to prevent:","tripping hazards",["extra revenue","guest complaints about price","late checkout"],"Clear paths reduce accidents.")
H("603.d.3.B",3,"If a guest slips in the lobby, an employee should help and then complete an:","incident report",["menu","timesheet","invoice"],"Incidents must be documented.")
H("603.d.3.B",4,"Reporting accidents promptly helps a hotel respond to injuries and reduce future:","risk",["revenue","staff","guests"],"Reports show where hazards exist.")
H("603.d.4.A",3,"An employee who keeps a guest's room number and personal details private is maintaining client:","confidentiality",["enthusiasm","punctuality","speed"],"Privacy protects guests.")
H("603.d.4.A",4,"Telling a stranger on the phone which room a celebrity guest is in would violate:","confidentiality",["scheduling","inventory","grooming"],"Guest security depends on discretion.")
H("603.d.4.B",3,"Staying on task, finishing assigned duties, and helping others are signs of a strong:","work ethic",["rumor","grudge","excuse"],"Ethic shows in everyday effort.")
H("603.d.4.B",4,"A worker with a strong work ethic who finishes early will usually:","ask what else needs doing",["leave quietly","sit idle","take a long break"],"Initiative adds value.")
H("603.d.4.C",3,"Returning extra change handed to you by mistake is an act of:","integrity",["theft","greed","laziness"],"Honesty means doing right when no one is watching.")
H("603.d.4.C",4,"Which action shows professional integrity?","admitting a mistake and correcting it",["hiding the error","blaming a coworker","ignoring the problem"],"Integrity includes accountability.")
H("603.d.4.D",3,"A hotel's acceptable-use policy says employees may not use work computers for:","personal gaming",["guest registration","email to vendors","room assignments"],"These policies limit non-work activity.")
H("603.d.4.D",4,"Using polite language and professional tone in business emails to guests is part of technology:","etiquette",["hardware","wiring","pricing"],"Good manners apply online too.")
H("603.d.4.E",3,"Following fire codes, health regulations, and labor laws is part of complying with:","rules, laws, and regulations",["gossip","trends","coupons"],"Compliance keeps a business legal and safe.")
H("603.d.4.E",4,"A hotel that ignores fire exit requirements risks fines and danger to:","guests and staff",["only owners","only suppliers","only inspectors"],"Regulations exist to protect people.")
H("603.d.5.A",3,"During a hospitality practicum, a student should keep a log to document and evaluate daily:","learning activities",["meal costs","parking tickets","bus rides"],"Documentation shows what was learned.")
H("603.d.5.A",4,"A supervised practicum differs from a regular class because students work under the guidance of a(n):","workplace supervisor",["random stranger","guest","vendor"],"Supervisors direct and evaluate on-the-job learning.")
H("603.d.5.B",3,"A student at the front desk who enters a guest's name, dates, and room preference is practicing:","registration procedures",["laundry procedures","menu design","payroll tasks"],"Registration records stay details of the stay.")
H("603.d.5.B",4,"Choosing a room and linking it to a guest's reservation is called room:","assignment",["service","dismissal","design"],"Room assignment matches guests with rooms.")
H("603.d.5.C",3,"Using words like 'folio,' 'turndown,' and 'walk-in' correctly on the job shows command of job-specific:","vocabulary",["menus","fabrics","maps"],"Technical terms speed up communication.")
H("603.d.5.C",4,"A guest without a reservation who asks for a room at the desk is called a:","walk-in",["no-show","upgrade","comp"],"Walk-ins arrive unannounced.")
H("603.d.5.D",3,"A student who accurately and quickly completes all tasks in a hotel department shows:","proficiency",["boredom","hesitation","confusion"],"Proficiency means competent performance.")
H("603.d.5.D",4,"Learning to coordinate the daily cleaning schedule shows proficiency in the duties of a hotel's:","housekeeping department",["sales team","finance office","security desk"],"Each department has its own tasks.")
H("603.d.5.E",3,"Photos, completed checklists, and supervisor notes are examples of representative work:","samples",["debts","rumors","gifts"],"Samples show real skills in action.")
H("603.d.5.E",4,"Collecting work samples during a practicum helps a student build a:","portfolio",["budget","lease","contract"],"Samples are used to show employers what you can do.")

# ---- 604 Event and Meeting Planning (part A) ----
H("604.d.1.A",3,"An event planner who joins a professional association and takes industry workshops is working toward career advancement and lifelong:","learning",["rivalry","silence","spending"],"Ongoing learning keeps skills current.")
H("604.d.1.A",4,"Earning a certified meeting professional credential is a strategy to enhance a planner's:","career prospects",["vacation days","office size","parking space"],"Credentials signal expertise to employers.")
H("604.d.1.B",3,"A global health emergency that cancels large gatherings shows how historical events can reshape the:","event industry",["weather forecast","school calendar","tax code"],"Major events change how planners work.")
H("604.d.1.B",4,"After a major disruption, planners often add virtual and hybrid options, which shows how history drives:","industry change",["price freezes","menu repeats","staff vacations"],"Planners adapt to new realities.")
H("604.d.1.C",3,"A planner prepares a backup indoor space in case a storm threatens an outdoor wedding. This is a plan that addresses current:","conditions",["menus","uniforms","trophies"],"Plans respond to what is happening now.")
H("604.d.1.C",4,"When travel prices rise sharply, a planner might respond by choosing a closer venue or offering a:","virtual option",["longer agenda","bigger budget","dress code"],"Good plans adapt to current events.")
H("604.d.1.D",3,"A planner keeps vendor contracts as scanned files and a printed binder. This documents knowledge in electronic and:","manual formats",["verbal formats only","secret formats","random formats"],"Records can be stored on paper and on a computer.")
H("604.d.1.D",4,"Keeping a digital checklist of past events helps a planner reuse what worked, which is a form of documenting:","technical knowledge",["rumors","guest gossip","menu fonts"],"Written records preserve know-how.")
H("604.d.1.E",3,"A student prepares a collection of resumes, event plans, and photos from past events to present to employers. This is a professional:","portfolio",["invoice","contract","budget"],"Portfolios showcase experience.")
H("604.d.1.E",4,"When presenting a portfolio, the best order is usually to start with your strongest items and explain your:","role in each project",["salary demands","favorite foods","weekend plans"],"Employers want to know what you contributed.")
H("604.d.1.F",3,"A candidate compares two planner jobs: one pays more, and the other includes health coverage and training. The candidate is comparing salaries and:","benefits",["rumors","menus","venues"],"Total pay includes benefits.")
H("604.d.1.F",4,"A job paying $48,000 with no benefits versus $46,000 plus paid insurance might be worth the same or more because benefits add:","value",["debt","tax","risk"],"Insurance and time off carry real worth.")
H("604.d.1.G",3,"A planner tracks monthly pay, rent, and food to see how much can go to savings. This is a personal:","budget",["agenda","floor plan","guest list"],"Budgets plan income and spending.")
H("604.d.1.G",4,"A planner paid irregularly by event should set aside money in busy months to cover slower ones, which is part of personal:","money management",["event marketing","venue scouting","sponsor relations"],"Irregular income needs careful planning.")
H("604.d.2.A",3,"Introducing guests properly, using titles, and saying 'thank you' to vendors are examples of professional:","etiquette",["accounting","décor","catering"],"Etiquette shows respect.")
H("604.d.2.A",4,"At a formal dinner, the host usually stands to greet arriving guests, showing proper social:","manners",["math","pricing","budgeting"],"Correct manners help guests feel welcome.")
H("604.d.2.B",3,"Using a clear subject line and a polite greeting in an email to a client is correct electronic communication:","etiquette",["tax","price","menu"],"Online messages should be courteous.")
H("604.d.2.B",4,"Typing in all capital letters in a business email can seem like:","shouting",["whispering","politeness","humor"],"All caps comes across as rude.")
H("604.d.2.C",3,"A hospitality code of ethics asks professionals to treat everyone fairly and protect:","client information",["their own profits only","their competitors","gossip"],"Codes guide honest conduct.")
H("604.d.2.C",4,"A code of ethics for the profession is meant to guide planners in situations where the right action is:","not obvious",["always clear","irrelevant","illegal"],"Codes help with difficult choices.")
H("604.d.2.D",3,"A vendor offers a planner a private gift in exchange for choosing their services over cheaper ones. The most ethical course is to:","decline and disclose it",["accept quietly","hide it from the client","raise the price"],"Conflicts of interest should be avoided or revealed.")
H("604.d.2.D",4,"When two choices both seem acceptable, the most ethical choice is the one that is honest, fair, and:","protects the client",["saves the planner time","earns a bonus","hides risks"],"Ethics puts others' interests alongside your own.")
H("604.d.3.A",3,"A planner who finishes tasks early, keeps files neat, and does not quit when a problem arises shows organization and:","perseverance",["rivalry","avoidance","gossip"],"Perseverance means sticking with the task.")
H("604.d.3.A",4,"Essential workplace traits for planners include dependability, flexibility, and:","attention to detail",["arrogance","idleness","secrecy"],"Small details make events succeed.")
H("604.d.3.B",3,"Assigning roles, sharing credit, and communicating openly help a planning team build:","trust",["conflict","delay","blame"],"Strong teams depend on trust.")
H("604.d.3.B",4,"A good team leader at an event briefing makes sure every member knows their:","role",["salary","hobbies","age"],"Clear roles prevent confusion.")
H("604.d.3.C",3,"By asking questions about a client's goals, guest count, and budget, a planner learns the client's:","needs",["hobbies","age","height"],"Questions uncover expectations.")
H("604.d.3.C",4,"A client says the event 'should feel elegant but not stuffy.' A planner responds well by asking for examples and:","clarifying details",["ignoring the comment","changing topics","assuming"],"Clarifying avoids misunderstandings.")
H("604.d.3.D",3,"Leadership on event day includes anticipating problems, such as a late caterer, and:","defusing them calmly",["ignoring them","panicking","blaming staff"],"Leaders stay calm and act.")
H("604.d.3.D",4,"A leader who notices a long registration line opens a second check-in table. This shows leadership by:","anticipating an issue",["delegating blame","cutting the budget","ignoring guests"],"Fixing a problem early prevents bigger ones.")
H("604.d.3.E",3,"A client wants live music, but the venue bans amplified sound. A planner can negotiate a compromise such as:","acoustic performers",["no entertainment","a larger venue fee","ignoring the rule"],"Negotiation seeks a solution both sides accept.")
H("604.d.3.E",4,"Which approach best resolves a conflict between a client and a vendor?","listen to both sides and find common ground",["pick the cheaper side","avoid both parties","blame the vendor"],"Win-win outcomes preserve relationships.")
H("604.d.4.A",3,"Terms like 'banquet event order,' 'load-in,' and 'attrition' are examples of event industry:","vocabulary",["recipes","fabrics","maps"],"Professionals share a common language.")
H("604.d.4.A",4,"The time vendors arrive to set up equipment before an event is called:","load-in",["breakdown","service","strike"],"Load-in is the setup arrival time.")
H("604.d.4.B",3,"A planner sends each vendor a written timeline so everyone arrives on time. This is a procedure to ensure client needs are:","met",["unknown","argued","delayed"],"Procedures make sure details are handled.")
H("604.d.4.B",4,"A site visit before booking a venue helps a planner confirm that the space fits the client's needs, capacity, and:","accessibility",["favorite colors","size of the logo","vendor's age"],"Visits reveal practical issues.")
H("604.d.4.C",3,"A company that controls costs, keeps a steady client base, and prices fairly is structured for:","profitability",["failure","closure","loss"],"Good structure supports profit.")
H("604.d.4.C",4,"A very small event company may keep costs low by outsourcing specialists as needed instead of hiring many:","full-time staff",["clients","vendors","planners"],"Flexible staffing reduces fixed costs.")
H("604.d.4.D",3,"Before an event, the planner and client sign a written agreement that spells out services, fees, and cancellation terms. This is a:","contract",["menu","invoice","receipt"],"Contracts protect both parties.")
H("604.d.4.D",4,"During an event, the planner follows the run-of-show, a minute-by-minute:","schedule",["recipe","budget","guest list"],"The run-of-show keeps the event on time.")
H("604.d.4.E",3,"Checking supply lists, confirming staff schedules, and reviewing the day's events are tasks for a planner's daily:","operations",["marketing","hiring","vacation"],"Organization keeps the office running.")
H("604.d.4.E",4,"The best way to organize daily work is to list tasks and rank them by:","urgency and importance",["alphabetical order","length of name","color"],"Prioritizing keeps deadlines.")
H("604.d.4.F",3,"The growth of online ticket sales and social media changed how events are advertised. This is a societal shift that shaped the:","industry",["calendar","weather","climate"],"Society's changes affect the business.")
H("604.d.4.F",4,"Increased interest in sustainability led many planners to reduce waste at events. This is an example of a:","societal trend",["tax cut","price freeze","new holiday"],"Public values shape practices.")
H("604.d.4.G",3,"A city organization that promotes tourism and helps groups find venues is a convention and visitors':","bureau",["bank","school","court"],"These bureaus help bring events to a city.")
H("604.d.4.G",4,"A convention and visitors' bureau can give planners destination information, hotel contacts, and:","local referrals",["tax returns","loans","passports"],"Bureaus connect planners with local resources.")
H("604.d.5.A",3,"Guests may have different dietary, language, and accessibility needs. These are the varying needs of:","customers",["suppliers","inspectors","banks"],"Planners serve diverse guests.")
H("604.d.5.A",4,"A client with guests using wheelchairs needs a venue with ramps and:","accessible restrooms",["steep stairs","narrow doors","low lighting"],"Accessibility is essential planning.")
H("604.d.5.B",3,"Respecting individual differences means treating each guest with:","courtesy and fairness",["indifference","impatience","bias"],"Respect applies to everyone.")
H("604.d.5.B",4,"A planner who learns that a guest cannot eat certain foods for religious reasons arranges a suitable menu. This shows respect for individual:","differences",["savings","tickets","dates"],"Honoring needs shows respect.")
H("604.d.5.C",3,"Meeting varying needs is important because it makes all attendees feel:","welcome",["excluded","ignored","confused"],"Inclusion improves the guest experience.")
H("604.d.5.C",4,"If a planner ignores special requests, the likely result is unhappy guests and a damaged:","reputation",["calendar","floor plan","budget line"],"Service quality builds a planner's name.")
H("604.d.5.D",3,"A business plan for an event company serving both corporate and wedding clients must address the needs of:","each market",["only one market","no market","competitors only"],"Plans should match audience needs.")
H("604.d.5.D",4,"A company that wants to attract clients from many cultures should plan for multilingual materials and flexible:","services",["pricing only","logos","parking"],"Business plans must be adaptable.")
H("604.d.5.E",3,"Greetings, gift giving, and dress expectations differ between cultures. These are differences in social:","etiquette",["inventory","taxes","wiring"],"Knowing customs prevents mistakes.")
H("604.d.5.E",4,"When planning an international business meeting, a planner should research local business customs, including:","greetings and dress",["weather only","sports scores","stock prices"],"Cultural research prevents offense.")

# ---- 604 Event and Meeting Planning (part B) ----
H("604.d.6.A",3,"Virtual reality venue tours and event apps are examples of emerging technologies that planners can use to:","improve the guest experience",["raise taxes","reduce guest count","cancel events"],"New tools help planners serve clients.")
H("604.d.6.A",4,"Before adopting a new technology, a planner should consider its cost, ease of use, and benefit to:","clients",["competitors","landlords","inspectors"],"Technology must serve a purpose.")
H("604.d.6.B",3,"A computer program that tracks registrations, budgets, and vendor contacts in one place is event planning:","software",["furniture","stationery","décor"],"It helps organize the work.")
H("604.d.6.B",4,"An advantage of using planning software over paper lists is that updates can be shared with the team:","instantly",["never","only monthly","by mail"],"Digital tools keep everyone current.")
H("604.d.6.C",3,"A slide show with video clips, music, and animation is a complex:","multimedia presentation",["written memo","phone call","table plan"],"Multimedia combines several media types.")
H("604.d.6.C",4,"When presenting to a client, crowded slides with too much text are less effective than clear visuals and:","brief key points",["long paragraphs","tiny fonts","dense tables"],"Simple slides communicate better.")
H("604.d.6.D",3,"At a trade show booth, the device that records sales and processes card payments is a point-of-sale:","system",["menu","license","badge"],"POS systems handle transactions.")
H("604.d.6.D",4,"An event organizer who uses a point-of-sale system can quickly see:","what sold",["guest ages","weather forecasts","vendor birthdays"],"POS data supports reports and decisions.")
H("604.d.6.E",3,"A planner decides to use the company website, email lists, and social media to sell tickets. These are Internet resources used to maximize:","profitability",["costs","delays","errors"],"Online tools reach more buyers.")
H("604.d.6.E",4,"A plan for using Internet resources should include goals, a schedule, and a way to measure:","results",["rumors","hobbies","moods"],"Measurement shows what works.")
H("604.d.6.F",3,"Sending quick updates to vendors through a group messaging tool is an electronic communication tool for:","planning",["subtraction","decoration","dancing"],"Digital tools speed communication.")
H("604.d.6.F",4,"An online registration form that collects payments is an electronic tool used for:","selling and planning",["cleaning only","cooking only","parking only"],"Forms handle sales and details.")
H("604.d.7.A",3,"A company that provides funding for an event in exchange for advertising is the event's:","sponsor",["vendor","guest","caterer"],"Sponsors provide financial support.")
H("604.d.7.A",4,"The person who coordinates the planning and day-to-day running of an event is the:","organizer",["attendee","sponsor","guest speaker"],"Organizers manage logistics.")
H("604.d.7.B",3,"A planner compares prices, quality, and reliability of rental companies before choosing a:","supplier",["guest","sponsor","banner"],"Selecting suppliers affects cost and quality.")
H("604.d.7.B",4,"Before signing with a supplier, the planner should check references and read the:","contract carefully",["menu twice","guest list","time zone"],"Contracts spell out obligations.")
H("604.d.7.C",3,"The person who sells event space and services to clients and works with them to book dates is a sales:","coordinator",["janitor","chef","driver"],"Sales coordinators build client relationships.")
H("604.d.7.C",4,"A sales coordinator's goals include booking events, answering client questions, and:","building repeat business",["discouraging inquiries","hiding fees","avoiding follow-up"],"Repeat clients are valuable.")
H("604.d.7.D",3,"If a client asks to cut catering costs, a planner may modify the menu by choosing less expensive:","dishes",["flowers","flights","fonts"],"Menu changes can fit the budget.")
H("604.d.7.D",4,"When evaluating catering options, a planner should compare price per person, quality, and ability to meet:","dietary needs",["birthday dates","parking limits","staff hobbies"],"Guests' needs shape choices.")
H("604.d.7.E",3,"Rows of chairs facing a speaker with no tables is called a theater-style or:","auditorium arrangement",["banquet arrangement","cabaret arrangement","boardroom arrangement"],"Seating style depends on the event.")
H("604.d.7.E",4,"For a training session where attendees take notes, a planner would usually choose which arrangement?","classroom",["theater","cocktail reception","open standing"],"Tables allow writing and materials.")
H("604.d.7.F",3,"A planner estimating how many servers, tables, and sound systems an event requires is determining the needed staff and:","resources",["rumors","gifts","taxes"],"Planning matches needs to supply.")
H("604.d.7.F",4,"If the guest count doubles, the planner must increase staff and supplies in proportion to meet the specific:","needs",["costs","fears","dates"],"Plans scale with demand.")
H("604.d.8.A",3,"In an event company, a team leader reports to a department head, who reports to the owner. These are different levels of management:","structure",["decor","menu","uniform"],"Management has levels from top to bottom.")
H("604.d.8.A",4,"The chain of command shows who a worker reports to and who has the authority to:","make decisions",["order lunch","set the weather","choose music only"],"Structure clarifies authority.")
H("604.d.8.B",3,"A resort offers scenery and lodging, but it is far from an airport. This is a disadvantage of the destination because guests may find it:","hard to reach",["too close","too cheap","too quiet to hear"],"Access affects attendance.")
H("604.d.8.B",4,"Convenient parking, nearby hotels, and meeting rooms are advantages that make a facility:","attractive to planners",["unusable","too accessible","less profitable"],"Facilities are chosen for convenience.")
H("604.d.8.C",3,"A company that employs its own event planner for internal meetings has an in-house:","event manager",["caterer","vendor","sponsor"],"In-house planners work for the organization.")
H("604.d.8.C",4,"An in-house planner's duties often include scheduling meetings, booking rooms, and managing the:","budget",["parking tickets","sports teams","landscaping"],"They support their own organization.")
H("604.d.8.D",3,"When working with an outside hotel for a conference, the planner's main role is to coordinate with the hotel's:","sales and catering staff",["laundry staff only","security vendors only","guests only"],"Planners and venues must communicate.")
H("604.d.8.D",4,"A planner and a venue manager confirm details in advance to avoid:","double booking and misunderstandings",["receiving revenue","cutting costs","saving time"],"Coordination prevents problems.")
H("604.d.9.A",3,"Venue rental, catering, and printing are examples of an event's:","expenses",["revenues","profits","grants"],"Expenses are costs of planning and production.")
H("604.d.9.A",4,"Adding up all planned costs before the event helps a planner create the event's:","budget",["floor plan","guest list","schedule"],"A budget compares costs with funds.")
H("604.d.9.B",3,"Offering an early-bird discount to boost ticket sales is a marketing technique that can improve:","profitability",["costs","waste","delays"],"Marketing brings in revenue.")
H("604.d.9.B",4,"A marketing technique like partnering with a local business to share promotions can reach new:","audiences",["landlords","regulators","banks"],"Partners expand reach.")
H("604.d.9.C",3,"A caterer charges $18 per person and 120 guests are expected. The cost of the meal is:","$2,160",["$1,800","$2,016","$216"],"18 times 120 equals 2,160.")
H("604.d.9.C",4,"Linens cost $4 each, and the event needs 45 tables with one linen per table. The total for linens is:","$180",["$49","$90","$225"],"4 times 45 equals 180.")
H("604.d.9.D",3,"Labor costs for hourly workers are called:","payroll expenses",["sales revenue","marketing costs","tax credits"],"Payroll affects profit.")
H("604.d.9.D",4,"Five workers each earn $15 an hour and work 6 hours. The payroll expense is:","$450",["$90","$75","$30"],"5 times 15 times 6 equals 450.")
H("604.d.9.E",3,"If an event runs over budget, the planner might modify operating procedures to cut waste, such as ordering supplies:","in bulk",["last minute","from anyone","twice"],"Procedures can be adjusted to control costs.")
H("604.d.9.E",4,"Changing the way staff set up tables so the job takes less time is a modification to operating:","procedures",["revenues","guests","vendors"],"Efficiency lowers cost.")
H("604.d.9.F",3,"A planner creating a marketing plan for weddings and government meetings must consider that each market has different:","needs and budgets",["time zones only","birthdays only","logos only"],"Different markets require different approaches.")
H("604.d.9.F",4,"Government clients often follow strict purchasing rules, so a marketing plan should highlight:","compliance and transparency",["flashy gifts","secrecy","lower quality"],"Government buyers value rules.")
H("604.d.9.G",3,"An event brings in $12,000 and costs $9,000. The profit is:","$3,000",["$21,000","$12,000","$9,000"],"12,000 minus 9,000 equals 3,000.")
H("604.d.9.G",4,"A profit margin of 25 percent on $20,000 in sales means the profit is:","$5,000",["$25,000","$500","$4,000"],"25 percent of 20,000 is 5,000.")
H("604.d.9.H",3,"Surveying guests after an event is a(n):","post-event evaluation",["pre-event evaluation","contract review","tax filing"],"Feedback shows what worked.")
H("604.d.9.H",4,"A pre-event evaluation checks readiness, such as confirming vendors, while a post-event evaluation reviews:","what happened and results",["next year's menu","staff birthdays","parking prices"],"Both support improvement.")
H("604.d.10.A",3,"Liability insurance protects an event organizer from costs if a guest is injured. The amount the insurance will pay is a liability:","limit",["tax","menu","fee"],"Policies set coverage limits.")
H("604.d.10.A",4,"A venue may require a planner to carry at least $1 million in insurance. This shows why planners must understand coverage:","requirements",["trends","rumors","tickets"],"Venues set insurance minimums.")
H("604.d.10.B",3,"If a client supplies their own insurance policy for an event, the planner must verify that it covers the date, location, and:","type of event",["guest names","caterer's fees","music playlist"],"Coverage must match the event.")
H("604.d.10.B",4,"Some venues allow clients to buy one-day event coverage, which protects against property damage and:","guest injuries",["menu errors","traffic","weather forecasts"],"One-day policies are common.")
H("604.d.10.C",3,"Planners must ensure fire exits are clear, food is safe, and capacity is not exceeded to meet legal, health, and safety:","obligations",["rumors","trends","habits"],"Safety is a legal duty.")
H("604.d.10.C",4,"Posting a venue's maximum occupancy and not allowing more guests to enter helps meet safety:","regulations",["goals","fashions","hobbies"],"Capacity limits protect people.")
H("604.d.10.D",3,"Hosting an event where drinks are served can make the host legally responsible if a guest is hurt after drinking. This is a legal:","implication",["discount","advantage","holiday"],"Providing alcohol creates liability.")
H("604.d.10.D",4,"To reduce risk at an event that serves alcohol, a planner can hire trained servers, check IDs, and arrange safe:","transportation",["parking fees","décor","entertainment"],"Responsible service reduces harm.")
H("604.d.10.E",3,"Large public events often need coordination with police and fire officials for crowd control and emergency access. These are law enforcement:","requirements",["rumors","gifts","trends"],"Authorities set rules for public safety.")
H("604.d.10.E",4,"A planner of a street festival typically applies for a permit and meets city safety and traffic:","rules",["debts","menus","trophies"],"Permits ensure public safety.")

